INSERT INTO `verse` VALUES (149943,0,'chr','REV','21','','22','ᎬᏩᎦᏘᏯ ᎤᏓᏙᎵᏍᏗ ᎨᏒ ᎤᎬᏫᏳᎯ ᏥᏌ ᎦᎶᏁᏛ ᎢᎦᏤᎵᎦ ᎢᏤᎳᏗᏙᎮᏍᏗ ᏂᏥᎥᎢ. ᎡᎺᏅ.'),(147737,0,'chr','2CO','18','','5','ᎠᎴ ᏂᎦᏗᏳ ᏧᏓᎴᏅᏛ ᎤᏁᎳᏅᎯ ᎢᏳᏩᏂᏌᏛ, ᎾᏍᎩ ᏙᎯ ᏥᏄᏩᏁᎸ ᎡᏗᏍᎦᎩ ᎨᏒ ᏥᏌ ᎦᎶᏁᏛ ᎠᎬᏗᏍᎬᎢ, ᎠᎴ ᎠᏴ ᎣᎦᏒᎦᎶᏔᏅ ᏙᎯ ᎢᎬᏁᎯ ᏗᎦᎸᏫᏍᏓᏁᏗ;'),(145531,0,'chr','JHN','21','','14','ᎾᏍᎩ Ꮎ ᏗᎧᎿᏩᏛᏍᏗ ᎠᏆᏤᎵᎦ ᎤᏍᏆᏂᎪᏗ ᎠᎴ ᏗᎧᎿᏩᏕᎩ, ᎾᏍᎩ ᎠᏴ ᎠᎩᎨᏳᎯ, ᎠᎴ ᎠᏴ ᎠᎩᎨᏳᎯ ᎤᎨᏳᎯ ᎨᏎᏍᏗ ᎡᏙᏓ, ᎠᎴ ᎠᏴ ᏥᎨᏳᎢᏳ ᎨᏎᏍᏗ, ᎠᎴ ᎬᏂᎨᏒ ᏅᏓᏥᏯᏛᏁᎵ.'),(143327,0,'chr','MAK','22','','7','ᎦᏃᏍᎩᏛ ᎨᏒᎢ, ᏧᎬᏩᎶᏗ ᎠᎬᎥᎯᏍᏗ ᎨᏒᎢ, ᎤᏲ ᎢᏯᏛᏁᏗ ᎨᏒᎢ, ᎦᎶᏄᎮᏛ ᎨᏒᎢ, ᎠᎵᏐᏢᎢᏍᏙᏗ ᎨᏒᎢ, ᎠᏛᏳᎨᏗ ᎨᏒᎢ, ᎠᏓᏐᏢᎢᏍᏙᏗᏱ, ᎠᏢᏉᏙᏗᏱ, ᎠᎵᏍᎦᎿᏫᏍᏗ ᎨᏒᎢ.'),(10488,0,'asv','GEN','37','','30','And Jacob took him rods of fresh poplar, and of the almond and of the plane-tree. And peeled white streaks in them, and made the white appear which was in the rods.'),(12694,0,'asv','LEV','21','','13','But if the priest look on it, and, behold, there be no white hairs therein, and it be not lower than the skin, but be dim; then the priest shall shut him up seven days:'),(14900,0,'asv','DEU','7','','13','of the gods of the peoples that are round about you, nigh unto thee, or far off from thee, from the one end of the earth even unto the other end of the earth;'),(17106,0,'asv','1SM','25','','12','But if ye shall still do wickedly, ye shall be consumed, both ye and your king.'),(19312,0,'asv','2KG','17','','6','And Elisha prayed, and said, Jehovah, I pray thee, open his eyes, that he may see. And Jehovah opened the eyes of the young man; and he saw: and, behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha.'),(21518,0,'asv','2CH','22','','32','Thus Jehovah saved Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem from the hand of Sennacherib the king of Assyria, and from the hand of all [others], and guided them on every side.'),(23724,0,'asv','PS','11','','16','Thou wilt show me the path of life: In thy presence is fulness of joy; In thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.           '),(25930,0,'asv','PS','4','','144','Man is like to vanity: His days are as a shadow that passeth away.'),(28136,0,'asv','ISA','10','','43','Ye are my witnesses, saith Jehovah, and my servant whom I have chosen; that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I am he: before me there was no God formed, neither shall there be after me.'),(30342,0,'asv','EZE','13','','13','Therefore thus saith the Lord Jehovah: I will even rend it with a stormy wind in my wrath; and there shall be an overflowing shower in mine anger, and great hailstones in wrath to consume it.'),(32548,0,'asv','ZEC','5','','4','Then the angel that talked with me answered and said unto me, Knowest thou not what these are? And I said, No, my lord.'),(34754,0,'asv','LUK','26','','5','And amazement took hold on all, and they glorified God; and they were filled with fear, saying, We have seen strange things to-day.'),(36960,0,'asv','ACT','2','','12','And he killed James the brother of John with the sword.'),(39166,0,'asv','COL','3','','4','withal praying for us also, that God may open unto us a door for the word, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I am also in bonds;'),(41372,0,'bbe','GEN','58','','24','And they sent for Rebekah and said to her, Are you ready to go with this man? And she said, I am ready.'),(43578,0,'bbe','LEV','6','','6','Then let him take to the Lord the offering for his wrongdoing; giving to the priest for his offering, a male sheep from the flock, without any mark, of the value fixed by you:'),(45784,0,'bbe','DEU','8','','5','You may not make for yourselves an image in the form of anything in heaven or on earth or in the waters under the earth:'),(47990,0,'bbe','1SM','27','','2','And a man of God came to Eli and said to him, The Lord says, Did I let myself be seen by your father\'s people when they were in Egypt, servants in Pharaoh\'s house?'),(50196,0,'bbe','1KG','22','','21','And I will make your family like the family of Jeroboam, the son of Nebat, and like the family of Baasha, the son of Ahijah, because you have made me angry, and have made Israel do evil.'),(52402,0,'bbe','2CH','2','','24','And Joash did what was right in the eyes of the Lord as long as Jehoiada the priest was living.'),(54608,0,'bbe','JOB','21','','40','He takes his rest under the trees of the river, and in the pool, under the shade of the water-plants.'),(56814,0,'bbe','PS','2','','122','At last our feet were inside your doors, O Jerusalem.'),(59020,0,'bbe','ISA','18','','33','Your heart will give thought to the cause of your fear: where is the scribe, where is he who made a record of the payments, where is he by whom the towers were numbered?'),(61226,0,'bbe','EZE','1','','3','And he said to me, Son of man, take this roll for your food, and go and say my words to the children of Israel.'),(63432,0,'bbe','NAH','10','','2','Everything has been taken from her, all is gone, she has nothing more: the heart is turned to water, the knees are shaking, all are twisted in pain, and colour has gone from all faces.'),(65638,0,'bbe','LUK','22','','1','And when he came out he was not able to say anything, and they saw that he had seen a vision in the Temple; and he was making signs to them without words.'),(67844,0,'bbe','ACT','5','','7','And God gave him no heritage in it, not even enough to put his foot on: but he gave him an undertaking that he would give it to him and to his children after him, though he had no child at that time.'),(70050,0,'bbe','EPH','23','','5','For the husband is the head of the wife, as Christ is the head of the church, being himself the saviour of the body.'),(72256,0,'dar','GEN','7','','18','And Abraham ran to the herd, and took a calf tender and good, and gave [it] to the attendant; and he hasted to dress it.'),(74462,0,'dar','EXO','4','','38','And he made for the altar a grating of network of copper under its ledge from beneath, to the very middle of it.'),(76668,0,'dar','NUM','27','','34','and for the tribe of the children of Asher, a prince, Ahihud the son of Shelomi;'),(78874,0,'dar','JUG','25','','19','But the men would not hearken to him; and the man took his concubine, and brought her forth to them; and they knew her, and abused her all the night until the morning; and let her go when the morning-dawn arose.'),(81080,0,'dar','1KG','6','','15','And there had been war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam all the days of his life.'),(83286,0,'dar','2CH','8','','13','And now ye think to shew yourselves strong against the kingdom of Jehovah in the hand of the sons of David; and ye are a great multitude, and ye have with you the golden calves that Jeroboam made you for gods.'),(85492,0,'dar','JOB','17','','33','That he may withdraw man [from his] work, and hide pride from man.'),(87698,0,'dar','PS','4','','118','Oh let them that fear Jehovah say, that his loving-kindness [endureth] for ever.'),(89904,0,'dar','ISA','2','','23','Be still, ye inhabitants of the isle! The merchants of Sidon, that pass over the sea, have replenished thee.'),(92110,0,'dar','JER','9','','52','And they took the king, and brought him up to the king of Babylon, unto Riblah in the land of Hamath, and he pronounced judgment upon him.'),(94316,0,'dar','AMO','10','','8','And I will turn your feasts into mourning, and all your songs into lamentation; and I will bring up sackcloth upon all loins, and baldness upon every head; and I will make it as the mourning for an only [son], and the end thereof as a bitter day.'),(96522,0,'dar','MAK','25','','12','For when they rise from among [the] dead they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as angels [who are] in the heavens.'),(98728,0,'dar','JHN','6','','21','And he said to them, Cast the net at the right side of the ship and ye will find. They cast therefore, and they could no longer draw it, from the multitude of fishes.'),(100934,0,'dar','GAL','10','','3','For as many as are on the principle of works of law are under curse. For it is written, Cursed is every one who does not continue in all things which [are] written in the book of the law to do them;'),(103140,0,'wbt','GEN','10','','9','And with every living creature that is with you, of the fowl, of the cattle, and of every beast of the earth with you, from all that go out of the ark, to every beast of the earth.'),(105346,0,'wbt','EXO','1','','31','And the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,'),(107552,0,'wbt','NUM','19','','29','And one kid of the goats for a sin-offering; besides the continual burnt-offering, and its meat-offering, and their drink-offerings.'),(109758,0,'wbt','JUG','4','','11','And it came to pass in process of time, that the children of Ammon made war against Israel.'),(111964,0,'wbt','1KG','54','','8','And it was so, that when Solomon had made an end of praying all this prayer and supplication to the LORD, he arose from before the altar of the LORD, from kneeling on his knees, with his hands spread up to heaven.'),(114170,0,'wbt','2CH','16','','3','And he made chains, as in the oracle, and put them on the heads of the pillars; and made a hundred pomegranates, and put them on the chains.'),(116376,0,'wbt','JOB','15','','24','The eye also of the adulterer waiteth for the twilight, saying, No eye shall see me: and disguiseth his face.'),(118582,0,'wbt','PS','6','','106','We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.'),(120788,0,'wbt','ISA','13','','10','For he saith, By the strength of my hand I have done it, and by my wisdom; for I am prudent: and I have removed the bounds of the people, and have robbed their treasures, and I have put down the inhabitants like a valiant man:'),(122994,0,'wbt','JER','24','','46','The daughter of Egypt shall be confounded; she shall be delivered into the hand of the people of the north.'),(125200,0,'wbt','HOS','9','','13','O Israel, thou hast destroyed thyself; but in me is thy help.'),(127406,0,'wbt','MAK','18','','7','And he saith to them, Are ye so void of understanding also? Do ye not perceive, that whatever thing from without entereth into the man, it cannot defile him.'),(129612,0,'wbt','JHN','19','','14','Yet a little while, and the world seeth me no more; but ye see me: because I live, ye shall live also.'),(131818,0,'wbt','2CO','16','','5','Wherefore henceforth we know no man according to the flesh: though indeed we have known Christ according to the flesh, yet now henceforth we know him no more.');

